This repo is managed using GNU Stow which allows me to automatically symlink
everything into place.

If you want to use these files, you have to clone it into ~/.dotfiles, cd into
there, and then run  stow common linux  if you're on Linux, or  stow common
macos  if you're on Mac from the folder. After that, .stowrc will be set up for
you and you can just use  stow  from anywhere and it will use the correct flags.

The options I use are --dotfiles, which will link a filename beginning with dot-
into an actual dotfile, and --no-folding, which won't link entire folders (so
files added later to those folders don't end up accidentally in the repo). The
target is also automatically set to ~, so if you want to stow it to somewhere
else, you need to specify -t. Similar, if you clone to anywhere other than
~/.dotfiles, you need to specify -d, or edit common/dot-stowrc.

All files and script are licensed under CC0 / Kopimi <https://kopimi.com/>, so I
encourage everyone to fork, copy, share, remix, enjoy and have fun with
everything you see.
